(text "DESIGN NOTES" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 200.66 114.3 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3a78d5cd-4d8e-52de-80ab-c374f6b7b7ee"))
(text "1  Supply: 12 V from Mean Well GST90A12-P1M (12 V +/-5 %, 6.67 A, 2.5 x 5.5 mm centre-positive plug) into J1.
   Build A: J2 passes 12 V to the Jetson Orin Nano carrier DC jack J16 (9-20 V input, 3.5 A max).
   Build B: J2 not fitted; Raspberry Pi 5 runs from the Raspberry Pi 27 W USB-C Power Supply.
2  Logic is 3.3 V throughout. Jetson J12 signals pass through TXB0108 translators: external pull-ups
   and pull-downs on those pins must be weaker than 50 kOhm. R1-R3 are 100 kOhm. U2 buffers the header
   so the 20 kOhm EN pull-up inside the driver module never loads a header pin.
3  Power-up state: R3 holds EN_IN high, U2 drives ~{EN} high, motor outputs off until software drives
   EN_IN low. STEP_IN and DIR_IN idle low (R1, R2).
4  Driver mode: MS1 = MS2 = VIO -> 1/16 step, interpolated to 1/256 µsteps. SPREAD = GND -> stealthChop
   (silent; the microphones share the enclosure). UART jumper pins left open.
5  Motor current: set the module trimmer to VREF = 1.41 V (0.11 Ohm sense; 2.50 V = 1.77 A RMS)
   -> 1.00 A RMS, the QSH4218-41-10-035 rated phase current.
6  D1 (VIO -> VM) and C1 (100 µF low-ESR at the driver) follow Watterott's SilentStepStick power guidance.
   VM (12 V) is present before VIO (+3V3 from the SBC), the order Watterott specifies.
7  Homing: DRV5032FA samples at 20 Hz. Software homes the Earth ring at a speed that keeps the magnet
   within the switch threshold for at least 100 ms (two samples).
8  Motor wiring (ADI QSH4218 datasheet Table 4.1): black A, green A-, red B, blue B-.
" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 200.66 119.38 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "4e94e40b-09b3-54c6-8f23-35875a9c7083"))
